  "note": "From the ford across 泓水 (northriver/midriver/southriver.c: chest-deep and cold, the current turning at the narrows where boats go down, a corner of 山烟寺 already in sight) to 江南渡口 and its jetty; up the rough yellow-earth path round the foot of 日照山 (road1-4.c), east to 乔阴; onto the mountain road of great mossy stones under the cliff carved 「山烟寺」 (sroad1.c), round the bend (sroad2.c) to the 山门 in the temple's golden-roofed wall (gate.c: 金碧辉煌) and west into the tunnel cut through the cliff, smelling of sulphur. Old: the stones worn, the path rutted, the gate's gilt dulled.",
